          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+field+theory"} Euclidean field theory
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propagators"} propagators
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correlators"} correlators
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributions+of+several+variables"} distributions of several variables
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singularities"} singularities
            on the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fat+diagonal"} fat diagonal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+of+distributions"} pull-back
            these distributions to
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
            on (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fulton-MacPherson+compactifications"} Fulton-MacPherson compactifications
            of)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+spaces+of+points"} configuration spaces of points
            and regard them in this incarnation, in particular discuss their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} renormalization
            from this perspective.
          %p
            Analogous to the perspective of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wavefront+sets"} wavefront sets
            for distributions, this perspective amounts to recording around each potentially singular point an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"} (d-1)-sphere
            worth of extra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direction+of+a+vector"} directional
            information carried by the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correlator"} correlator
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+amplitude"} Feynman amplitude
            in the vicinity of the point.
          %p
            This approach goes back to
            %a{:href => "#AxelrodSinger93"} Axelrod-Singer 93
            in the discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization+of+Chern-Simons+theory"} quantization of Chern-Simons theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+complex"} graph complex
            of
            %a{:href => "#Kontsevich94"} Kontsevich 94
            (full details due to
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#LambrechtsVolic14"} Lambrechts-Volić 14
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+algebra"} de Rham algebra
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+points"} configuration space of points
            is actually
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphic
            to all possible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+amplitudes"} Feynman amplitudes
            for free
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AKSZ+theory"} AKSZ theory
          %p
            A general and systematic discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative quantum field theory
            and its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} renormalization
            from this perspective is offered in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Berghoff14a"} Berghoff 14a
            %a{:href => "#Berghoff14b"} Berghoff 14b
            (albeit presently only for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+quantum+field+theory"} Euclidean quantum field theory
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relativistic+quantum+field+theory"} relativistic quantum field theory
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#higher_chernsimons_theory Higher Chern-Simons theory
          %p
            This approach to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pQFT"} pQFT
            was originally considered specifically for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+propagator"} Chern-Simons propagator
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization+of+3d+Chern-Simons+theory"} quantization of 3d Chern-Simons theory
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#AxelrodSinger93"} Axelrod-Singer 93
            %a{:href => "#BottCattaneo97"} Bott-Cattaneo 97, Remark 3.6
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#CattaneoMnev10"} Cattaneo-Mnev 10, Remark 11
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Chern-Simons+theory"} higher Chern-Simons theory
            such as notably the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AKSZ+sigma-models"} AKSZ sigma-models
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+propagator"} Feynman propagator
            depends only on the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free field theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d A = 0
            in all these cases.
          %p
            Here the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+propagator"} Chern-Simons propagator
            regarded as a non-singular
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fulton-MacPherson+compactification"} compactification
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+points"} configuration space of points
            serves to exhibit its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+amplitudes"} Feynman amplitudes
            as providing
            = succeed "-models" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+complex"} graph complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
            of these
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fulton-MacPherson+compactification"} compactified
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+spaces+of+points"} configuration spaces of points
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Kontsevich94"} Kontsevich 94
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#Kontsevich93"} Kontsevich 93, 5
